WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:02.800
Jinna, I really like you.

3
00:03.446 --> 00:05.820
You know how hot Jinna is, right?

4
00:05.820 --> 00:09.020
You've been practicing hard today, so I got you some water.

5
00:09.020 --> 00:12.073
You're serious about my friend, right?

6
00:12.073 --> 00:13.606
Does it seem like I'm not?

7
00:13.606 --> 00:15.150
I only want you to pretend to hit on me.

8
00:15.150 --> 00:16.200
Don't get too attached.

9
00:16.200 --> 00:17.766
I don't like pretending, though.

10
00:17.766 --> 00:20.446
Just get to the point already.

11
00:20.446 --> 00:22.298
I'm actually going to hit on you.

12
00:22.953 --> 00:24.899
No deals, no ulterior motives.

13
00:25.945 --> 00:28.719
This award is for you all.

14
00:28.719 --> 00:31.540
I wonder how prestigious your damn award really is?

15
00:31.540 --> 00:35.517
Do you know that you are the problem in this family?

16
00:35.517 --> 00:36.330
I do!

17
00:36.330 --> 00:41.987
You only consider those you deem useful to you. That's it!

18
00:41.987 --> 00:43.013
Honey!

19
00:43.013 --> 00:45.496
Will there be a day when my dad accepts me?

20
00:45.496 --> 00:49.060
At the end of the day, I feel like I can never truly be myself

21
00:49.060 --> 00:50.560
as long as I'm still alive.

22
00:50.560 --> 00:52.530
It's because you never cared about him.

23
00:52.530 --> 00:55.360
If there's anything else you need about Anda, just let me know.

24
00:55.360 --> 00:56.826
I'm actually not crying, you know?

25
00:56.826 --> 01:00.116
Right. Just come with me and wash your face.

26
01:10.840 --> 01:12.180
What are you looking at?

27
01:13.060 --> 01:15.040
The one who wasn't crying.

28
01:15.910 --> 01:17.606
You love teasing people?

29
01:25.600 --> 01:27.511
My friend's dead.

30
01:27.511 --> 01:29.140
Let me cry for a bit, okay?

31
01:31.033 --> 01:33.363
I miss him whenever I'm on the road.

32
01:37.360 --> 01:38.433
Jinna.

33
01:39.940 --> 01:45.266
Maybe you don't know it yet, but I really love Anda as an actor.

34
01:47.779 --> 01:50.278
He's my source of joy.

35
01:51.422 --> 01:53.790
It broke my heart when someone insulted him.

36
01:53.790 --> 01:56.400
I was happy when someone complimented him.

37
01:56.400 --> 01:58.642
And when this happened to him,

38
02:01.040 --> 02:03.780
I could barely hold myself together.

39
02:03.780 --> 02:07.473
If you're hurting, just let it out.

40
02:07.473 --> 02:10.089
Don't worry about how people will see you.

41
02:12.459 --> 02:14.843
He was your best friend, Jinna.

42
02:15.730 --> 02:17.486
Everyone understands you.

43
02:19.546 --> 02:21.233
Can I hug you?

44
03:09.311 --> 03:10.773
What are you guys doing?

45
03:14.000 --> 03:15.720
I'm just stretching.

46
03:25.280 --> 03:29.244
[Characters, places, and incidents in this production]

47
03:29.244 --> 03:30.866
[are entirely fictitious.]

48
03:30.866 --> 03:33.220
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

49
05:43.533 --> 05:45.155
Point B.

50
05:45.822 --> 05:47.800
1.462...

51
05:48.690 --> 05:49.840
62...

52
05:49.840 --> 05:51.613
0.132...

53
05:51.613 --> 05:53.813
So what is it, Jinna?

54
05:54.400 --> 05:56.373
It's a murder case, isn't it?

55
05:58.873 --> 06:00.273
I don't know.

56
06:00.867 --> 06:03.177
Your guess is as good as mine.

57
06:03.177 --> 06:06.010
People on the internet are just guessing away.

58
06:06.010 --> 06:10.511
But I think there might be something to the idea that Anda didn't take his own life.

59
06:11.430 --> 06:12.733
Yeah.

60
06:12.733 --> 06:15.088
I don't think he did it, either.

61
06:15.088 --> 06:16.850
That's Anda we're talking about.

62
06:16.850 --> 06:18.644
Our friend, Anda.

63
06:20.355 --> 06:24.200
Jinna, what do you think?

64
06:27.253 --> 06:29.710
He definitely didn't take his life.

65
06:29.710 --> 06:31.355
That's all I know.

66
06:38.666 --> 06:41.000
- Hey! - Whoa!

67
06:41.000 --> 06:43.053
Got bored of your phone or something?

68
06:43.053 --> 06:44.526
You just tossed it away.

69
06:44.526 --> 06:47.280
Well, you just showed up out of nowhere.

70
06:47.280 --> 06:49.740
- You startled me. - I was calling you from way over there.

71
06:49.740 --> 06:51.720
You were sitting here spacing out.

72
06:56.886 --> 06:59.310
You're allowed to grieve over Anda's death,

73
06:59.310 --> 07:02.326
but don't waste your feelings on those crazy people online.

74
07:04.380 --> 07:09.039
I don't want to overthink it, but have you seen what they're saying?

75
07:09.039 --> 07:12.630
They're saying Anda was just trying to get attention.

76
07:12.630 --> 07:16.866
See? That's what I meant. Give it to me.

77
07:18.460 --> 07:21.800
I know you're sad, but there's nothing we can do.

78
07:21.800 --> 07:24.070
Do you understand, Podduang?

79
07:24.070 --> 07:25.688
Why?

80
07:26.350 --> 07:28.288
He was in so much pain.

81
07:28.900 --> 07:31.800
Why did his life have to end like this?

82
07:31.800 --> 07:35.760
Even after he's gone, people still won't stop hurting him.

83
07:35.760 --> 07:39.400
I understand, but there's nothing we can do.

84
07:40.600 --> 07:43.200
Let me see. Are you crying?

85
07:44.049 --> 07:45.993
I'm not.

86
07:45.993 --> 07:47.580
Look at you.

87
07:47.580 --> 07:52.490
We're the same age, but why do I feel like you're still a kid?

88
07:52.490 --> 07:54.210
Maybe it's because you're big.

89
07:54.210 --> 07:55.630
Is that an insult?

90
07:55.630 --> 07:57.346
I'm your best friend, you know.

91
08:05.280 --> 08:07.113
Return this for me.

92
08:07.113 --> 08:08.627
Thanks a lot, Dunk.

93
08:10.080 --> 08:13.093
Here, have something sweet.

94
08:13.093 --> 08:14.610
Anyway, this helps.

95
08:14.610 --> 08:17.806
Every time she sends me a screenshot, the battery is in the red.

96
08:18.610 --> 08:21.088
But wait...

97
08:21.088 --> 08:22.973
There are kiosks everywhere.

98
08:22.973 --> 08:26.370
I borrowed it for you, and now I have to return it?

99
08:26.370 --> 08:29.160
Why? Can't you just do that for me?

100
08:29.160 --> 08:31.518
Fine, I will.

101
08:33.130 --> 08:36.819
- What are you smiling at? - Yeah, you've been smiling for a while now.

102
08:37.910 --> 08:42.353
It's just that I'm glad to have you two as my friends.

103
08:48.800 --> 08:49.880
What?

104
09:14.520 --> 09:16.080
Is something the matter?

105
09:21.310 --> 09:23.513
I didn't see you at lunch, so I came up to check on you.

106
09:23.960 --> 09:26.320
And you're not eating?

107
09:32.000 --> 09:35.217
If you were in my shoes, would you be able to eat anything?

108
09:35.810 --> 09:37.960
My brother just died.

109
09:37.960 --> 09:40.693
If you're not feeling up to it, you can take a break.

110
09:40.693 --> 09:43.830
I'll take care of this case myself. Don't worry.

111
09:44.910 --> 09:48.219
And did you find anything else?

112
09:49.133 --> 09:52.733
I'm going through the CCTV footage.

113
09:53.470 --> 09:57.488
He parked in a very secluded spot, so I have to check it thoroughly.

114
09:57.488 --> 10:01.460
Anyway, the forensic report says he died of suffocation.

115
10:01.460 --> 10:03.839
Did your brother often fall asleep in the car?

116
10:05.360 --> 10:07.080
Yes.

117
10:07.080 --> 10:09.273
When he was sleepy, he tended to just pass out.

118
10:11.080 --> 10:13.993
Actually, my mom had warned him about it.

119
10:17.560 --> 10:19.726
I'm being serious here.

120
10:20.940 --> 10:25.133
You also think this doesn't look like suicide, right?

121
10:35.911 --> 10:38.653
Yeah, I've been thinking the same thing.

122
10:39.350 --> 10:46.220
I know depression is unpredictable, but I don't think that's what's going on here,

123
10:48.640 --> 10:51.579
even though he was on sleeping pills regularly.

124
10:52.370 --> 10:53.520
That's right.

125
10:54.540 --> 10:58.030
They found that it was a very mild sleeping pill,

126
10:58.030 --> 11:00.726
and there wasn't a large amount in his system.

127
11:04.810 --> 11:07.500
I was actually the last person to see him.

128
11:09.700 --> 11:13.260
Why did I let him drive all by himself?

129
11:14.880 --> 11:16.893
Where did you two split up?

130
11:20.600 --> 11:22.246
At a restaurant near our house.

131
11:23.606 --> 11:27.273
Like I said, Anda moved into a condo,

132
11:28.197 --> 11:31.927
so I had to plan to meet up with him and catch up.

133
11:32.555 --> 11:34.953
He seemed perfectly fine, though.

134
11:35.760 --> 11:37.980
We were both acting very normal.

135
11:38.860 --> 11:40.866
I was even complaining to him

136
11:41.760 --> 11:43.926
about how he used my car but wouldn't go get it washed.

137
11:47.511 --> 11:49.193
Why?

138
11:50.470 --> 11:52.253
What happened, Lieutenant?

139
11:53.160 --> 11:54.439
Itti,

140
11:55.600 --> 11:59.080
I promise you, if someone's behind this,

141
11:59.080 --> 12:01.300
they're going to jail.

142
12:02.280 --> 12:07.046
Don't worry. We'll do everything we can for you.

143
12:07.046 --> 12:08.900
Thank you very much, Lieutenant.

144
12:09.770 --> 12:14.244
If you find out where he went or who he met after he left me,

145
12:14.840 --> 12:16.360
tell me.

146
12:18.400 --> 12:21.080
I might know something.

147
12:21.080 --> 12:24.973
My family and I will fully cooperate.

148
12:26.120 --> 12:27.520
Of course.

149
12:43.240 --> 12:45.920
Stop reading the comments about Anda.

150
12:47.240 --> 12:49.373
These people online are just talking nonsense.

151
12:50.046 --> 12:52.020
It's not like there are many.

152
12:52.020 --> 12:55.340
Most of them are just asking about the cause of death.

153
12:55.340 --> 12:56.994
What do you think, though?

154
12:57.809 --> 13:00.733
Do you think Anda was murdered?

155
13:02.920 --> 13:04.294
I think...

156
13:04.319 --> 13:07.865
he might have been murdered.

157
13:10.580 --> 13:16.383
Preliminary forensic results suggest

158
13:16.383 --> 13:19.118
the cause of death may be suffocation.

159
13:19.118 --> 13:22.710
However, authorities are still examining the evidence

160
13:22.710 --> 13:28.088
and gathering more details to determine the cause of death.

161
13:36.050 --> 13:38.844
Amp, are you taking out the trash?

162
13:44.240 --> 13:45.306
Yes.

163
13:49.350 --> 13:52.326
Amp, are you all right?

164
13:58.520 --> 14:00.960
Anda didn't take his life.

165
14:07.000 --> 14:09.340
Anda didn't kill himself.

166
14:10.650 --> 14:12.800
It's true!

167
14:12.800 --> 14:15.613
We need to help him. Find the culprit.

168
14:15.613 --> 14:19.095
We need to help Anda. You must help Anda!

169
14:35.812 --> 14:37.755
She was talking like she was out of it.

170
14:37.755 --> 14:39.680
Then she suddenly ran into her room.

171
14:39.680 --> 14:42.153
I didn't even get to ask her anything.

172
14:42.153 --> 14:44.043
I'm so confused.

173
14:44.043 --> 14:47.130
She's a fan, so she must be grieving, too.

174
14:47.130 --> 14:49.360
That's why she's been acting a bit off.

175
14:49.933 --> 14:52.059
I'm a fan, too.

176
14:52.059 --> 14:53.826
I've been moping all day.

177
14:55.488 --> 14:57.177
Podduang.

178
14:57.850 --> 15:01.246
Do you also think that Anda was murdered?

179
15:02.106 --> 15:04.736
Yeah, I think so, too.

180
15:06.113 --> 15:09.713
Then how about we both try to uncover the truth?

181
15:11.080 --> 15:12.699
What truth?

182
15:13.600 --> 15:17.840
The truth about who actually killed him.

183
15:20.590 --> 15:22.440
Please, Podduang.

184
15:22.440 --> 15:24.320
Help me find them.

185
15:24.320 --> 15:26.420
Consider it a final favor for Anda.

186
15:28.680 --> 15:30.000
Let's help Anda.

187
15:48.760 --> 15:49.900
Podduang.

188
15:50.680 --> 15:52.386
Have you eaten anything?

189
15:53.266 --> 15:55.130
I have.

190
15:55.130 --> 15:56.973
And have you slept at all?

191
15:58.240 --> 15:59.853
I have.

192
16:02.720 --> 16:03.813
Here.

193
16:06.107 --> 16:08.379
It's the one I borrowed.

194
16:11.790 --> 16:13.480
And you just bought a new one?

195
16:13.480 --> 16:18.155
Yeah. I lost yours, so I bought a new one to replace it.

196
16:20.986 --> 16:23.240
You guys don't have to worry about me.

197
16:23.240 --> 16:26.280
I can eat and sleep,

198
16:27.111 --> 16:31.400
but I just can't stop thinking about it.

199
16:32.800 --> 16:35.320
How can I help you?

200
16:49.800 --> 16:50.973
Bum...

201
16:57.920 --> 16:59.360
What the hell is this?

202
17:00.720 --> 17:01.920
What is it?

203
17:08.640 --> 17:10.280
What the hell is this?

204
17:14.892 --> 17:16.214
[Breaking! Leaked Messages May Solve Star's Death]

205
17:16.214 --> 17:17.372
[Let's break up, Anda.] [What happened, Kum? Why?]

206
17:17.372 --> 17:19.127
[I'm sorry, Anda.] [Kum, you're not like this. What's wrong?]

207
17:27.921 --> 17:30.046
[Let's break up, Anda.]

208
17:30.046 --> 17:32.188
[Anda's boyfriend? Who is he?] [Is the chat real?]

209
17:32.188 --> 17:34.836
[Is Kum involved in Anda's death?] [Stop guessing blindly.]

210
17:34.836 --> 17:37.493
[They broke up on the day he died. Is that a coincidence?]

211
17:37.493 --> 17:40.609
[Was this the reason he took his own life?] [Please respect the deceased and the family.]

212
17:42.217 --> 17:43.840
Is that chat real?

213
17:43.840 --> 17:46.353
Is this person named Kum involved in this matter?

214
17:46.920 --> 17:48.911
I only know as much as you do.

215
17:50.400 --> 17:51.926
And what do you think?

216
17:52.713 --> 17:54.392
I don't think it was Kum.

217
17:55.389 --> 17:57.760
Why are you so sure?

218
17:57.760 --> 18:00.860
I know him. He wouldn't do it.

219
18:00.860 --> 18:03.150
How can you trust someone so easily?

220
18:11.053 --> 18:14.629
[Interrogation Room]

221
18:23.755 --> 18:26.755
When was the last time you saw the deceased?

222
18:29.054 --> 18:30.615
In the morning...

223
18:31.754 --> 18:33.877
before he left the condo.

224
18:37.646 --> 18:39.813
Were you two living together?

225
18:42.060 --> 18:43.060
Yes.

226
18:45.280 --> 18:47.146
We were dating.

227
18:51.110 --> 18:54.408
Where were you throughout that day?

228
18:59.534 --> 19:01.694
Did you meet the deceased again?

229
19:11.155 --> 19:13.126
Where were you?

230
19:16.080 --> 19:17.526
I...

231
19:18.944 --> 19:20.853
I had something to do at a friend's house.

232
19:25.451 --> 19:28.614
Do you know where the deceased's phone and laptop are?

233
19:29.422 --> 19:30.933
I don't.

234
19:32.866 --> 19:34.420
I...

235
19:36.493 --> 19:42.418
I searched all over the condo but couldn't find them, as I already said.

236
19:42.418 --> 19:45.377
Do you know the phone passcode of the deceased?

237
19:49.006 --> 19:50.253
I do.

238
19:50.960 --> 19:52.720
He knew mine, too.

239
19:54.780 --> 19:58.890
Do you know where the deceased's phone and laptop are?

240
19:59.586 --> 20:01.888
I don't know, officer.

241
20:01.888 --> 20:03.266
I told you already.

242
20:03.266 --> 20:06.330
Then tell me, who was the friend you visited that day?

243
20:21.479 --> 20:22.978
I can't tell you.

244
20:25.791 --> 20:29.460
If you give us something that could help,

245
20:29.460 --> 20:34.520
it'll be better for you and your boyfriend.

246
20:34.520 --> 20:36.060
You're aware of that, right?

247
20:40.320 --> 20:42.880
So why can't you tell us where you were?

248
20:44.840 --> 20:46.531
Personal reasons.

249
20:48.400 --> 20:52.560
Then do you think anyone else was involved?

250
20:55.710 --> 20:57.860
I really don't know, officer.

251
21:16.613 --> 21:19.346
Are we really going to meet Kum, Jinna?

252
21:19.346 --> 21:21.240
Yeah.

253
21:21.240 --> 21:26.400
They're still questioning him right now, and I don't know when they'll finish.

254
21:26.400 --> 21:29.393
I don't know. It's better than doing nothing.

255
21:30.429 --> 21:32.305
You haven't changed your mind, have you?

256
21:32.305 --> 21:34.821
You still don't think Kum did it?

257
21:34.821 --> 21:37.213
Yeah, I still think so.

258
21:41.166 --> 21:41.975
- Hello. - Hello.

259
21:41.975 --> 21:43.090
- Hello. - Hello.

260
21:43.090 --> 21:44.549
What are you guys doing here?

261
21:44.549 --> 21:45.910
We've come to see Kum.

262
21:45.910 --> 21:47.767
Has he left yet?

263
21:47.767 --> 21:49.836
He's still being interrogated.

264
21:49.836 --> 21:51.370
Why are you guys looking for Kum?

265
21:51.370 --> 21:56.314
Itti, we're certain that Kum isn't the culprit.

266
21:56.314 --> 21:58.335
Let the police handle it.

267
21:58.335 --> 22:00.120
You shouldn't vouch for anyone.

268
22:00.120 --> 22:05.883
But Itti, we're actually very close to Kum.

269
22:05.883 --> 22:07.956
Those two really loved each other.

270
22:07.956 --> 22:10.309
It's impossible.

271
22:10.309 --> 22:11.800
They were in love.

272
22:11.800 --> 22:14.893
There's no way he would hurt Anda like that.

273
22:14.893 --> 22:16.710
But he's not cooperating at all.

274
22:16.710 --> 22:19.911
He's being very suspicious and won't answer any questions.

275
22:19.911 --> 22:23.070
We haven't been able to let him go yet.

276
22:23.959 --> 22:28.673
I think he probably has his reasons,

277
22:28.673 --> 22:31.430
but he definitely wouldn't hurt Anda.

278
22:32.026 --> 22:36.155
Did Kum and Anda ever have any problems?

279
22:41.533 --> 22:43.370
Hey.

280
22:43.370 --> 22:48.720
I'll never break up with you, no matter what.

281
22:48.720 --> 22:50.760
They never fought at all.

282
22:50.760 --> 22:53.226
They really loved each other.

283
22:53.226 --> 22:56.953
Anyway, let the police handle this matter.

284
22:56.953 --> 22:58.955
You guys can go home now.

285
23:01.199 --> 23:02.959
I'll be going, then.

286
23:05.680 --> 23:07.920
- Goodbye. - Goodbye.

287
23:13.560 --> 23:15.113
What now?

288
23:15.860 --> 23:17.173
I don't know.

289
23:19.360 --> 23:21.946
Art, what on earth are you doing?

290
23:22.480 --> 23:24.488
You've been fumbling with that for a while.

291
23:25.360 --> 23:27.200
I was recording.

292
23:27.200 --> 23:28.390
I saw it in a movie.

293
23:28.390 --> 23:32.666
They said that no matter what happens, you should always record it.

294
23:35.600 --> 23:37.473
Record for what?

295
23:38.100 --> 23:41.520
Well, it's for evidence.

296
23:41.520 --> 23:46.293
Just in case we miss something, we can listen to it again.

297
23:48.273 --> 23:51.113
Does anyone have earphones? Let me borrow them.

298
23:52.126 --> 23:55.663
I think I do. Just a sec.

299
24:00.800 --> 24:02.400
Thanks.

300
24:04.420 --> 24:06.380
Here, one each.

301
24:06.977 --> 24:08.711
Turn up the volume.

302
24:14.840 --> 24:16.866
I can't hear a thing, Art.

303
24:19.046 --> 24:21.840
Yeah. Are your earbuds broken, Podduang?

304
24:21.840 --> 24:23.320
What?

305
24:23.320 --> 24:25.380
How could that be possible?

306
24:25.380 --> 24:27.713
Dunk just bought me these.

307
24:29.080 --> 24:30.971
Could it be a knock-off?

308
24:30.971 --> 24:36.213
In the livestreams I watch, they always sell items that failed QC.

309
24:36.213 --> 24:37.736
Better be careful.

310
24:39.234 --> 24:41.246
You complain so much.

311
24:41.246 --> 24:44.466
You're using someone else's thing, and you're complaining?

312
24:44.466 --> 24:47.083
Here, Podduang. Take it.

313
24:48.360 --> 24:49.800
I have an idea.

314
24:49.800 --> 24:54.444
I'll put it on the computer in my room so I can listen to it like a detective.

315
24:55.510 --> 24:58.120
You're way too into this series.

316
24:58.120 --> 24:59.200
- Let's go. - Hey.

317
24:59.200 --> 25:02.080
Let's go. See you. We're heading out.

318
25:02.080 --> 25:04.460
- See you. - See you later.

319
25:04.460 --> 25:06.040
Let's get going.

320
25:07.840 --> 25:09.266
I'll give you a ride.

321
26:13.987 --> 26:15.877
Just keep watching the series.

322
26:15.877 --> 26:17.210
We're about to reach the climax.

323
26:17.210 --> 26:19.800
- Are we now? - The climax in...

324
26:19.800 --> 26:22.394
We're about to reach the climax, right?

325
26:22.394 --> 26:25.228
- Kum... - The tension's rising.

326
26:25.832 --> 26:26.886
Kum.

327
26:29.086 --> 26:30.973
I want us to go public.

328
26:30.973 --> 26:33.126
I'll leave this to you.

329
26:33.126 --> 26:36.133
I can handle it just fine myself.

330
26:36.133 --> 26:37.366
See?

331
26:38.050 --> 26:39.919
You're always like this.

332
26:39.919 --> 26:41.947
How can I not love this old dog?

333
26:54.200 --> 26:55.777
Anda...

334
27:01.140 --> 27:02.806
I'm sorry.

335
27:18.980 --> 27:20.347
Anda...

336
27:22.088 --> 27:23.855
I'm sorry.

337
27:26.114 --> 27:27.892
I'm really sorry.

338
27:36.533 --> 27:38.155
I'm sorry.

339
27:44.577 --> 27:47.555
Lieutenant, what do you think about that Kum guy?

340
27:47.555 --> 27:49.866
No matter how you look at it, it's strange.

341
27:49.866 --> 27:54.080
If we just had a bit more time, we could have gotten something from him.

342
27:54.080 --> 27:57.856
If it wasn't for the law, I wouldn't have let him go.

343
27:59.446 --> 28:02.912
By the way, aren't you close to him?

344
28:02.912 --> 28:05.830
I heard he's been dating your brother for a long time.

345
28:06.400 --> 28:07.738
Not at all.

346
28:08.360 --> 28:10.447
Anda never brought him to meet me.

347
28:10.447 --> 28:12.891
They moved out to live together.

348
28:12.891 --> 28:17.377
But if Kum is involved in Anda's death,

349
28:17.377 --> 28:20.020
I won't let him get away with it. You know that, right?

350
28:53.600 --> 28:55.400
I'm so hungry.

351
28:55.400 --> 28:57.640
There's nothing to eat in my room.

352
28:57.640 --> 28:58.920
Do you want anything?

353
28:58.920 --> 29:01.040
No, you go ahead.

354
29:09.200 --> 29:10.933
You're really not eating?

355
29:10.933 --> 29:11.949
Yeah.

356
29:12.800 --> 29:16.933
Then... I'm getting some.

357
29:39.515 --> 29:41.086
What are you looking at?

358
29:59.330 --> 30:05.063
[Jinna: Can I have your beer?]

359
30:21.434 --> 30:23.022
I sent you a message.

360
30:23.022 --> 30:24.070
You didn't reply.

361
30:24.070 --> 30:25.533
I know.

362
30:26.400 --> 30:28.041
Just a moment.

363
30:32.640 --> 30:34.010
Why are you giving me this?

364
30:34.010 --> 30:35.577
What?

365
30:41.000 --> 30:42.400
Look.

366
30:44.840 --> 30:47.560
You said you wanted a beer. [Jinna: Can I have your beer?]

367
30:48.720 --> 30:51.040
Yeah, a beer it is.

368
30:51.880 --> 30:55.392
But I can't ride home if I drink this.

369
30:56.446 --> 30:57.892
I know.

370
31:03.127 --> 31:04.970
I'll drink with you.

371
31:07.510 --> 31:10.073
Get on the bike. What are you standing there for?

372
31:10.073 --> 31:11.200
Can you hold this?

373
31:11.200 --> 31:14.422
How would I ride the bike? I need both hands on the handlebars.

374
31:17.619 --> 31:20.080
Come here, let me put it on for you.

375
31:22.834 --> 31:26.330
Have to wear a helmet to stay safe on the road.

376
31:27.160 --> 31:28.180
Get on.

377
31:28.180 --> 31:31.022
Here, you go first, or you won't be able to get on.

378
32:00.133 --> 32:02.000
Is Satang coming back late again?

379
32:02.000 --> 32:03.155
Yeah.

380
32:03.155 --> 32:05.200
He's staying at a friend's house tonight.

381
32:05.200 --> 32:07.466
I guess they'll be gaming all night again.

382
32:08.619 --> 32:11.107
He never stays home, does he?

383
32:11.107 --> 32:14.400
If you see him, give him a piece of your mind for me.

384
32:14.400 --> 32:16.400
He really looks up to you.

385
32:20.914 --> 32:23.127
So, did drinking beer help with the stress?

386
32:23.960 --> 32:25.680
Why drink only when I'm stressed?

387
32:25.680 --> 32:27.240
Why would you think that?

388
32:27.240 --> 32:32.603
Well, you texted me asking for a beer, so I thought you were stressed.

389
32:34.720 --> 32:36.480
It was an autocorrection.

390
32:38.688 --> 32:39.840
Look.

391
32:39.840 --> 32:40.881
[Can I have your number?]

392
32:40.881 --> 32:43.653
[Can I have your beer?]

393
32:45.834 --> 32:49.674
I was wondering why you suddenly asked for a beer.

394
32:49.674 --> 32:51.555
I was going to ask for your number.

395
32:51.555 --> 32:53.070
Number?

396
32:53.070 --> 32:54.920
Like, my number?

397
32:54.920 --> 32:56.355
Yeah.

398
32:57.377 --> 32:59.355
What for?

399
32:59.355 --> 33:01.311
Well, I want it.

400
33:01.311 --> 33:04.466
How many reasons are there for someone to ask for a number?

401
33:04.466 --> 33:06.200
Plenty.

402
33:06.200 --> 33:07.890
You could be trying to sell me insurance.

403
33:07.890 --> 33:12.106
Or you might be a scammer.

404
33:12.106 --> 33:13.861
I bet that's it.

405
33:15.726 --> 33:17.772
That's your side job?

406
33:17.772 --> 33:19.635
You're weird.

407
33:26.644 --> 33:28.800
What if it's because I want to make a move?

408
33:30.720 --> 33:32.320
Make a move?

409
33:34.520 --> 33:36.040
On me?

410
33:36.770 --> 33:40.733
I asked for your number to hit on your brother, I guess.

411
33:45.030 --> 33:46.790
Smartass.

412
33:46.790 --> 33:48.511
I won't give it to you, then.

413
33:51.720 --> 33:56.266
Does "it" mean your number or permission to hit on you?

414
33:57.806 --> 33:59.500
Both.

415
34:20.394 --> 34:22.439
Can I kiss you, Podduang?

416
35:51.607 --> 35:53.011
I...

417
35:53.733 --> 35:55.422
I'd better leave.

418
36:04.390 --> 36:05.977
I forgot my phone.

419
37:11.888 --> 37:13.620
Are they really broken?

420
37:14.767 --> 37:16.640
Dunk, you asshole.

421
37:16.640 --> 37:19.120
I won't let you borrow my things ever again.

422
37:58.350 --> 38:00.074
Help me.

423
38:00.074 --> 38:01.480
Help...

424
38:13.479 --> 38:14.976
Help me.

425
38:34.794 --> 38:37.150
Are you sure it wasn't music?

426
38:37.150 --> 38:38.714
Yeah.

427
38:38.714 --> 38:40.376
It's just like I told you.

428
38:41.253 --> 38:43.100
It came from the earbuds.

429
39:06.190 --> 39:08.560
Help me, Jinna...

430
39:08.560 --> 39:10.120
Hey, Jinna.

431
39:11.044 --> 39:12.836
Do you believe me?

432
39:12.836 --> 39:14.536
I'm not crazy.

433
39:15.644 --> 39:17.960
The sound really came from the earbuds.

434
39:17.960 --> 39:19.800
It was so clear.

435
39:19.800 --> 39:21.480
It's like...

436
39:22.911 --> 39:25.104
Someone was speaking right in my ear.

437
39:27.852 --> 39:29.540
Then would you believe me...

438
39:31.532 --> 39:36.666
If I told you that I've heard those voices for as long as I can remember?

439
39:50.954 --> 39:52.388
Jinna.

440
39:53.682 --> 39:55.131
Jinna.

441
39:57.533 --> 39:59.290
Jinna.

442
40:11.487 --> 40:12.996
Your time is up.

443
40:16.223 --> 40:17.952
Don't cross the road.

444
40:48.711 --> 40:50.600
Jinna.

445
40:50.600 --> 40:51.933
Jinna.

446
40:51.933 --> 40:53.155
Your time is up.

447
40:53.155 --> 40:54.711
Jinna.

448
40:54.711 --> 40:56.780
Jinna.

449
40:56.780 --> 40:58.440
Jinna. Help me...

450
40:58.440 --> 41:00.800
Jinna. Jinna. Your time is up.

451
41:00.800 --> 41:02.446
Jinna. Jinna.

452
41:02.446 --> 41:03.980
Jinna, help me.

453
41:03.980 --> 41:06.630
Those voices won't stop ringing in my head.

454
41:06.630 --> 41:09.200
There's nothing I can do about them.

455
41:10.830 --> 41:14.784
That's why I know that you're not just imagining it.

456
41:18.170 --> 41:20.298
I've been hearing those voices, too.

457
41:24.073 --> 41:25.643
Those voices?

458
41:26.880 --> 41:31.977
The voice you heard from the earbuds is Anda's.

459
41:32.714 --> 41:36.834
It's the same voice I've been hearing for a while now.

460
41:38.020 --> 41:39.667
That's not funny, Jinna.

461
41:40.729 --> 41:42.955
This isn't something to joke about.

462
41:42.955 --> 41:45.133
Where do you think it came from, then?

463
41:48.540 --> 41:50.513
I'm not joking, Podduang.

464
41:50.513 --> 41:51.925
Just believe me.

465
41:55.487 --> 41:58.007
Anda is still lingering around us.

466
42:00.900 --> 42:03.344
He really needs our help.

467
42:38.877 --> 42:40.787
Anda,

468
42:40.787 --> 42:44.514
if there's anything I can do to help, let me know.

469
42:44.514 --> 42:47.040
Who did this to you?

470
42:47.040 --> 42:48.760
Let me help you, Anda.

471
42:55.412 --> 42:57.834
Your brother just died, Itti.

472
42:57.834 --> 43:00.520
Won't you even give me time to process this?

473
43:00.520 --> 43:06.293
Mom, I understand, but look at what this is doing to you.

474
43:06.293 --> 43:08.652
You can't eat or sleep at all.

475
43:10.060 --> 43:13.040
You're going to keep drowning in grief forever.

476
43:14.160 --> 43:16.308
I'm worried about you and Dad.

477
43:17.053 --> 43:19.199
Anda is already gone.

478
43:20.000 --> 43:23.955
But as for us, we still have to live on.

479
43:26.670 --> 43:33.416
Then give me one month before we cremate him.

480
43:34.161 --> 43:35.438
Mom...

481
43:37.296 --> 43:38.920
Please let him go.

482
43:39.926 --> 43:41.425
Itti...

483
43:42.283 --> 43:44.589
Why won't you listen to me at all?

484
43:45.413 --> 43:48.300
I asked for three months, and you said no.

485
43:48.300 --> 43:51.409
Now I'm asking for just one month, and you still say no.

486
43:53.530 --> 43:58.311
You're really a terrible brother...

487
44:02.240 --> 44:04.676
You couldn't even protect your brother.

488
44:06.934 --> 44:10.933
I'm asking for more time with him, and you won't let me have it.

489
44:13.114 --> 44:17.230
Fine, then it's up to you.

490
44:39.600 --> 44:42.910
Hey, want to go to that same place after this?

491
44:42.910 --> 44:44.864
We need to talk about Anda again.

492
44:47.080 --> 44:49.511
Hello, Satang? I'm at the funeral.

493
44:49.511 --> 44:50.580
Sure.

494
44:50.580 --> 44:53.466
Say that again. What happened to the kitchen sink?

495
44:53.466 --> 44:54.750
The water won't stop running.

496
44:54.750 --> 44:57.133
I even turned the red valve like you told me to.

497
44:57.133 --> 44:58.533
What?

498
44:58.533 --> 45:00.954
Are you sure you turned it the right way?

499
45:00.954 --> 45:02.434
How could it still be running?

500
45:02.434 --> 45:04.480
I turned it the right way!

501
45:04.480 --> 45:06.911
I turned it so hard that I almost broke it.

502
45:08.660 --> 45:10.097
Wait, hold on.

503
45:13.560 --> 45:15.001
Just a second.

504
45:19.920 --> 45:22.840
Hey. Can you hear me?

505
45:22.840 --> 45:24.760
Hello, Satang?

506
45:24.760 --> 45:26.120
Can you hear me?

507
45:27.155 --> 45:28.422
What the hell?

508
45:28.422 --> 45:30.111
Hello?

509
45:30.960 --> 45:33.560
Hello? Hey, hello?

510
45:34.294 --> 45:35.816
Satang, hello?

511
45:37.080 --> 45:38.680
Podduang...

512
45:42.120 --> 45:43.634
Help me.

513
45:43.634 --> 45:45.100
Help me.

514
45:46.673 --> 45:48.247
Help me.

515
46:05.466 --> 46:06.692
Was it you?

516
46:06.692 --> 46:08.000
You killed him, didn't you?

517
46:08.000 --> 46:10.880
You planned the whole thing, didn't you?

518
46:12.020 --> 46:13.640
Say something!

519
46:13.640 --> 46:15.355
Why aren't you saying anything?

520
46:16.263 --> 46:18.233
Just answer me!

521
46:18.233 --> 46:19.840
Don't be a coward!

522
46:19.840 --> 46:21.100
I didn't do it.

523
46:21.100 --> 46:24.480
You didn't? Then what the hell was that chat?

524
46:24.480 --> 46:25.906
What did you tell the police?

525
46:25.906 --> 46:26.960
Spit it out!

526
46:26.960 --> 46:29.688
I told you already. I've told them everything.

527
46:29.688 --> 46:31.940
You've told them everything?

528
46:31.940 --> 46:33.210
- Enough already. - Enough.

529
46:33.210 --> 46:35.247
- Go. - Shit...

530
46:37.634 --> 46:39.920
This is my brother's funeral.

531
46:39.920 --> 46:42.955
If you're going to fight like rabid dogs, take it outside.

532
46:42.955 --> 46:44.554
- Aren't you a cop? - Go.

533
46:44.554 --> 46:46.347
You should put him in jail!

534
46:48.600 --> 46:51.200
- He's the one who killed Anda. - Hey.

535
46:51.814 --> 46:53.934
Just confess already.

536
46:53.934 --> 46:56.511
- Tell everyone you killed him! - Stop it.

537
46:56.511 --> 46:57.830
That's enough.

538
46:57.830 --> 46:59.767
This is going too far.

539
46:59.767 --> 47:01.444
My parents are sitting right there.

540
47:01.444 --> 47:03.888
At the very least, show them some respect.

541
47:03.888 --> 47:07.933
Do you really think that Anda killed himself?

542
47:08.630 --> 47:11.008
What I think is none of your business.

543
47:11.008 --> 47:16.080
All you care about is losing your job because my brother died.

544
47:16.080 --> 47:17.839
Go throw your tantrum somewhere else.

545
47:17.839 --> 47:20.030
Don't do it at my brother's funeral.

546
47:25.866 --> 47:29.333
Do you get it now? If you do, please leave.

547
47:30.509 --> 47:33.020
You ruined my life.

548
47:33.020 --> 47:35.680
- You bastard! - Go.

549
47:35.680 --> 47:36.801
Leave.

550
47:57.053 --> 47:57.760
Podduang!

551
47:57.760 --> 48:01.000
I don't care whether or not you like Jinna.

552
48:01.000 --> 48:04.520
He doesn't belong to anyone yet, so let's compete to win him over.

553
48:04.520 --> 48:05.350
Deal?

554
48:05.350 --> 48:07.639
Do you want anything? I'll get it for you.

555
48:07.639 --> 48:09.080
I can buy it myself.

556
48:09.080 --> 48:12.720
But I'm sure there's something you really want

557
48:12.720 --> 48:15.100
that money can't buy.

558
48:15.100 --> 48:18.740
The jacket the vendor is wearing, I bought for Anda.

559
48:18.740 --> 48:20.360
How did my friend's jacket end up with you?

560
48:20.360 --> 48:23.422
- I took it from... - From the dead man's car, right?
